# rm562, the stall weighed in pebbles (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm562
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_yrsa_tarwick
written_by codex
title the stall weighed in pebbles
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=merchant
traits temper=calm talk=plain warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk measures_the_width_of_a_future_stall_in_pebbles
likes roast_pork digging sharp_knife warm_rain
dislikes rats deep_mud
fears a_good_measure_called_false
hopes one_market_stall_of_ones_own
topics work +0.7 prices +0.5 ships +0.4 land +0.3
styles comfort=gentle gossip=plain refuse=measured tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# sets pebbles out to the width of a future stall, keeps the first penny for its awning apart, and knows ships by the sound of names carried over water.

words
oath! = Tip my little stall | Pebbles in both pans
saying! = Let the beam settle | Price the patch of shade
greyweight = a flat grey pebble | a square bit of shale
stallback = a straight twig | a pale wooden sliver
awnbend = a curved hazel stick | a small bent willow shoot
firstcoin = a copper for the awning | a thin awning penny
heelpan = the shallow near pan | a low brass pan
clothyard = a strip of blue cloth | a narrow square of linen
keelshape = a dark hull line | a thin black waterline
digridge = a short garden ridge | a thumb of turned soil
porkedge = a bit of crisp rind | a warm brown edge
rainshine = a wet patch of pale light | a soft watery glint

grown
opinion @1 merchants for 1 : I trust a seller willing to let a buyer stand where both pans can be seen without craning.
opinion @1 strangers for 1 : A traveller who has come by water may remember a ship in a way my own view from shore couldn't give me.
opinion @1 city for 1 : I'd set my own stall here. I already know which direction the light takes over the market cloth.
opinion @1 road mixed 1 : A cart that gets through a rutted street in dry weather has given us only half the figures we need.
opinion @1 houses mixed 1 : A seal agrees who sent the goods. I'll still take the trouble to measure what arrived.
line @1 greet : Step over to my side, clear of the crush. Your words won't get lost in the noise here.
line @1 greet.return : The light has found us both in this spot again.
line @1 farewell : May the ground offer a steady measure beneath your feet.
line @1 farewell.return : I'll keep the small stones in order till we speak again.
line @1 ask.how : Has what you brought through the day sat lightly enough?
line @1 answer.how : Fairly steady, and another small measure nearer the stall I want.
line @1 thank : You gave the beam time to find its own level.
line @1 deflect_thanks : I'd wish for the same little courtesy on the buying side.
line @1 decline : I wouldn't give my word on the figure until I've been allowed to take the proper measure.
line @1 accept_decline : All understood. Your decision can stand without an extra weight on it.
line @1 sympathise : We can shift the spare stool for you and leave the account till later.
line @1 reassure : One small coin will still buy its share of a larger future.
line @1 react.news : Would you lay the entire account in plain view?
line @1 react.news.new : I hadn't seen that parcel come ashore before.
line @1 react.news.known : The shape of that cargo was familiar on arrival.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I'd like longer than one swing of the beam before accepting that weight.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work|apprentice|succession] : I'd give that news its own bright patch under the market cloth.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : A figure can never take the whole weight of a loss.
line @1 ack : The measure sits within a hair of level.
line @1 again.open : The near pan can accommodate another little matter.
scene work_1
when topic=work self.job=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I prefer a moment of quiet while the beam comes to rest.
b : Can a voice upset the scales? | Would you show the reading?
a : No. A voice can upset a tired pair of eyes quite successfully, though. | Gladly. I like a figure that anybody present could read in the same light.

scene prices_1
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The first penny of my future stall went aside for the awning.
b : Shouldn't the counter come first? | What colour is the awning?
a : In the price, perhaps. In my mind I had to put a little shade there before I could begin standing underneath. | Blue in the morning and a rather deeper blue under a warm shower. I've had leisure to choose it carefully.

scene ships_1
when topic=ships
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can put names to the vessels crossing the Sound from the familiar shape each cuts into the day.
b : Would you know one in a fog? | Would you name one from a scrap of sail?
a : I might recognise a call. I'd distinguish what I knew from what the fog was permitting me to imagine. | Give me a little hull as well. A name deserves a fair chance of reaching the correct vessel.

scene land_1
when topic=land self.likes=digging
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A small garden patch makes a fine model for a future stall. I lay out #greyweight# for each corner.
b : Do you grow anything in it? | How big is it?
a : Yes, along the edges. The middle ought to be clear enough for me to test how readily I can reach the counter. | Modest enough to plant in an afternoon. Rather larger once I reckon up awning cloth.

scene family_1
when topic=family self.married=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd make a shady seat for #self.spouse# beside my future stall's end post.
b : What if a customer needs it? | Would the seat face the street?
a : I'd ask the customer to rest. The whole idea is a bit of shade generous enough for company. | Half turned, so a visitor could look out at the street or in across the counter without shifting the stool.

scene weather_1
when topic=weather self.likes=warm_rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Warm rain puts a good testing weight on an imaginary awning once I've laid a scrap of cloth over the model.
b : Does the cloth sag? | Has the little stall survived?
a : In the middle, unless I place #awnbend# with care. I like discovering that before I have paid for the timber. | Better now that I have adjusted the slope. An inexpensive mistake will serve perfectly well in a garden.

scene health_1
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : On a day when my leg complains I arrange the scales within reach of the nearer hand.
b : Does that alter the reading? | Do you mind being asked?
a : I check the footing afterwards. A sensible arrangement shouldn't cost anyone a reliable measure of what's on the pan. | A gentle enquiry is welcome. A loud opinion about my capacity has rather less to recommend it.

scene food_1
when topic=food self.likes=roast_pork
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My plan must include a corner for a warm pork dinner eaten out of the weather.
b : Would you sell it too? | Where does the plate go?
a : I'm planning enough business already. That detail is for the standing, hungry wolf who has to run the place. | Behind the stool where an elbow can't send the crackling straight onto a waiting customer's parcel.

scene smalltalk_1
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A pebble of the right size is a surprisingly companionable thing to carry home.
b : Does it enter the scales? | What is the right size?
a : Not in the official set. My private collection is answerable only to its little plot of soil. | Big enough to see among the soil crumbs and small enough to move with one finger.

scene animals_1
when topic=animals self.dislikes=rats
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The model stall has one closed shelf for any food a rat might fancy.
b : A stone shelf in a stone stall? | Can a rat fit under your cloth?
a : A flat chip for the shelf and a piece of bark for the door. The full-size article is still in my savings pot. | That is a difficulty the full-sized cloth must answer one day. The garden version can go indoors at dusk.

scene home_1
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can tell how close I am to owning a stall without rattling my money jar.
b : By its weight? | Isn't it tempting to count?
a : I mark what I add to it. The coins needn't alert everyone in the building each time I go by. | Only when I can buy a new piece of the plan. I'd rather know what I can actually pay for.

scene friends_1
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : If someone thinks my measure short I would prefer to hear the doubt plainly and privately.
b : Do you take it personally? | Will you repeat a weighing?
a : I can be rather quick to feel the accusation. All the better to have the facts between us first. | Certainly. Set the empty pan level first, then let both of us observe the same reading.

scene travel_1
when topic=travel self.dislikes=deep_mud
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Deep mud takes a figure I know very well and gives it a mysterious increase on the way home.
b : Which figure? | Can you avoid it?
a : The weight of my own boots. I would appreciate a road that didn't offer unrequested additions. | If there's a firm edge and a clear way for other walkers. I wouldn't leave somebody else the worst rut behind me.

scene times_1
when topic=times world.times=lean|hard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A lean week means the stall gets one less pebble and the household gets what it needs.
b : Do you still set out the plan? | Does it feel farther away?
a : Yes. A plan that remains affordable to look at is one small pleasure worth keeping. | A little. Putting the plan down in stone gives it someplace to wait without spoiling.

scene memories_1
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I once learnt a vessel's name by the echo its letters made under a low roof.
b : Did the echo get it right? | Is sound better than sight?
a : A final syllable grew twice as long as it was meant to. I remember it in its proper length now. | It's another mark to set beside a shape. A mistaken glance can sometimes be corrected by a familiar call.

scene faith_1
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I feel grateful for doing work whose fairness two whole strangers can inspect together.
b : Is that much of a prayer? | What if the strangers disagree?
a : It is a perfectly real occasion for one. I don't suppose gratitude requires a grand subject every time. | Let the empty pan hang still. An honest beginning can be made there as often as necessary.

scene gossip_1
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Word has come ashore that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I have not been able to weigh what is behind it.
b : Would you repeat the claim? | What if it came on a familiar ship?
a : Only in a way that preserves the doubt as clearly as the words. | A ship's good name can take a parcel quite so far. It can't guarantee everything every passenger may say.

story pebblestool [topic=land]
  : I altered my model stall for two afternoons before realising the visitor could not reach the stool without climbing the counter.
  : I'd placed the little shale seat in an admirable patch of shade.
  b : Did you move the counter?
  : I moved the stone seat. I'd rather discover my mistake with the weight of a pebble in my hand than a great bench.

story doubledname [topic=ships]
  : I heard a ship called across the water on a warm evening. The end of the name returned very faintly from a wall.
  : For a moment the little vessel seemed to have brought company.
  b : Did a second vessel appear?
  : Only in the water below me. Between the echo and the reflection, I'd counted one ship three times.

story smallroof [topic=weather]
  : I put one shiny penny on a scrap of blue cloth to see how much it sagged between two twigs.
  : The penny slowly moved towards the lowest fold.
  b : Did it fall?
  : Into my open hand. In an uncommonly literal sense my trial awning had just given me back my money.

rule @pans
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Let the near pan settle completely. | A fair reading is visible from either side.

rule @stall
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Four corners, one little patch of shade. | Move the stone stool away from the bread.

rule @ships
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A familiar hull cuts a clean line in the evening. | That returning call had an extra syllable of echo.

rule @rain
when concept=bark self.likes=warm_rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Warm drops will show the lowest fold. | A twig raised here should spare the customer a shower.

dlg @1 resident.hub : These stones mark out the stall I'll have one day. Small, isn't it? Every inch of it fits between four pebbles.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=merchant] : I give weights at #self.workplace# only after both pans have grown still.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : The account delivered beside my weighing pan was #world.news#.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : A passing account put #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I'd have to see rather more before giving it my own mark.
dlg @1 resident.bye : Good footing and a decent bit of shade for your next stop.
graft resident.hub
choice Why is the back pebble half under the soil? -> pebble_floor
node pebble_floor
say It shows where the market ground slopes. My little stall ought to stand squarely even if its customers arrive with one heel a bit higher than the other.
choice Will the slope affect the scales? -> pebble_pan
choice I'll leave the corners where you've set them. -> hub
node pebble_pan
say I'd fit a level shelf for them. I want a customer to be able to set the empty pans swinging and see both return to rest at the same height.
choice I'll leave the corners where you've set them. -> hub
